The SharedPreferences data is not deleted when the app is uninstalled because the SharedPreference data is stored in a persistent storage on the device. This is different from the data stored in the app's internal or external storage, which gets cleared when the app is uninstalled. SharedPreferences are designed to persist data across app restarts and even across app uninstalls and reinstalls. This is why you observe the data remaining intact after uninstalling and reinstalling the signed APK. 

To address this issue, you could consider implementing a check to see if the SharedPreferences data exists before assuming the user is already logged in. This way, you can prompt the user to log in again if the data is missing, ensuring a smoother user experience. 

Here's an example of how you might implement this:

```java
SharedPreferences sharedPreferences = getSharedPreferences("yourFileName", MODE_PRIVATE);
boolean isLoggedIn = sharedPreferences.getBoolean("isLoggedIn", false);

if (!isLoggedIn) {
    // Prompt user to log in again
    // Display login screen
} else {
    // User is logged in, proceed normally
}
```

By adding this check, you ensure that the app behaves correctly even when the SharedPreferences data is lost or corrupted, providing a more robust and user-friendly experience.

