To determine the protocol of a packet, you can read the Protocol field in the IP packet header. This field is located at the 4th position (0-based index) in the IP header. You can use the `struct ip` definition provided by the `arpa/inet.h` header file in C. Here's a simple example of how you might do this:

```c
#include <arpa/inet.h>

// Assume 'packet' is a pointer to the IP header
struct ip *ip = *(struct ip *)packet;

// Access the Protocol field
u_int8_t protocol = ip->h_proto;

// Now 'protocol' contains the protocol type of the packet
if (protocol == 6) {
    // It's a TCP packet
    // Handle TCP packet
} else if (protocol == 17) {
    // It's a UDP packet
    // Handle UDP packet
} else {
    // Unknown protocol
    // Handle unknown protocol
}
```

