Solution: Add [weak self] before any reference to self in your view controller class. This will ensure that when the view controller is deallocated, the reference to self is set to nil, preventing a retain cycle. For example:

    [weak self] _someViewController = new SomeViewController();
    _someViewController.SomeProperty = self;

Without this, if _someViewController holds a strong reference to self, then self will hold a strong reference to _someViewController, creating a retain cycle. This will prevent the view controller from being deallocated, causing it to accumulate memory over time.

